 On the svcnewsd account: it's not in our code. The credentials are stored on the ServiceNow platform side, in a Basic
  Auth Profile attached to the outbound REST Message "Chinou API" (password held encrypted, never visible to the
  script).

  Our Script Include just calls that REST Message by name. When the request runs, ServiceNow automatically attaches the
  svcnewsd credentials from the profile and routes the call through the MID server to Chinou. The Registration ID and
  model are read from system properties and added to the request body.

  So the account is used purely through the REST Message configuration — no username, password or token exists in the
  code.
